-- title:
--   Transport of linear parts under a centred Drinfeld chart isomorphism
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$. Let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain (complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal), $t_0$ an element of its maximal ideal, and $f_0,u_0,v_0 \in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ power series in two variables with $f_0 - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1)$ lying in $J_0^{q+2}$, where $J_0 = (X_0,X_1)$; let $W,t,f,u,v$ satisfy the same conditions, with $J = (X_0,X_1) \subseteq W[[X_0,X_1]]$. Put $S_0 = W_0[[X_0,X_1]]/(t_0v_0 - f_0u_0)$ and $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(tv - fu)$, with quotient map $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the latter. Assume given a ring isomorphism $\beta : S_0 \simeq S$ and a ring isomorphism $\beta_W : W_0 \simeq W$ such that $\beta$ carries the class of a constant $w$ to the class of the constant $\beta_W(w)$, and such that $\beta$ and $\beta^{-1}$ are centred, i.e. $\beta(X_j)$ lies in the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$ in $S$ and $\beta^{-1}(X_j)$ in the corresponding ideal of $S_0$, for $j = 0,1$. Assume further given a ring automorphism $\theta_0$ of $S_0$, a ring automorphism $\sigma_{W_0}$ of $W_0$ with $\sigma_{W_0}(w) - w$ in the maximal ideal for all $w$, such that $\theta_0$ sends the class of a constant $w$ to the class of the constant $\sigma_{W_0}(w)$, and a matrix $M_0 \in M_2(W_0)$ with $\theta_0(X_j) \equiv \sum_i (M_0)_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$ in $S_0$. Set $\theta = \beta \circ \theta_0 \circ \beta^{-1}$ on $S$ and $\sigma_W = \beta_W \circ \sigma_{W_0} \circ \beta_W^{-1}$ on $W$. The conclusion asserts the existence of matrices $B \in M_2(W)$, $B' \in M_2(W_0)$ and $M \in M_2(W)$ such that: $\beta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i B_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$; every entry of $B \cdot \beta_W(B') - 1$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$; $\theta$ sends the class of a constant $w$ to the class of the constant $\sigma_W(w)$; $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo that same squared ideal; and every entry of $M - B \cdot \beta_W(M_0) \cdot \beta_W(B')$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$, where $\beta_W$ is applied entrywise.
--
--   This is the comparison statement for linear parts of automorphisms of the local charts at a point of a Drinfeld-level modular curve: conjugating a semilinear automorphism by a centred isomorphism of charts preserves semilinearity, over the transported automorphism of the base, and changes the reduced linear part by conjugation by an invertible matrix over the residue field. It is used by the two transport theorems [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_semilinear_linearPart_transport_of_forall_specialLinearGroup_of_dense`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_semilinear_linearPart_transport_of_forall_specialLinearGroup_of_dense) and [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_semilinear_linearPart_transport_of_forall_specialLinearGroup_of_dense_of_prime`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_semilinear_linearPart_transport_of_forall_specialLinearGroup_of_dense_of_prime), where the matrix $B$ is subsequently constrained by a centraliser argument in $SL_2$.
